'' WHAT A BUILD PUTS ON DISK, which nothing could assert until EXPECT-FILE existed.
'' The runner captures tiko's stdout, and the result of '-dll' or '-lib' is a FILE --
'' so '-l'/'#inclib', '-mt''s archive choice and the whole of '-dll'/'-lib' were
'' verified by hand and recorded only in commit messages.
''
'' THE NAMES ARE fbc's, measured on the same sources:
''
''     -dll thing.bas               thing.dll  AND libthing.dll.a
''     -dll thing.bas -x custom.dll custom.dll AND libcustom.dll.a
''     -lib thing.bas               libthing.a
''
'' The import library follows the OUTPUT, not the source, which is why the second
'' line is worth stating separately.
''
'' TKO_LIBPATH points at the packaged runtime because a DLL still has to LINK --
'' this is a real build, not a dump. It replaces the bundled search rather than
'' adding to it, so the test says which libraries it means.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -lib tests/codegen/src/export.bas -o tests/driver/libexport.a
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0

'' The archive appears...
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/libexport.a

'' ...and nothing else does. '-lib' must not link: an archive is collected, not
'' linked, and running the linker demanded a main the library has no business
'' carrying -- lld-link said 'subsystem must be defined', which is it asking what
'' kind of PROGRAM this is.
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: tests/driver/libexport.exe
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: tests/driver/libexport.dll
